\section{Discussion and Conclusion}

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Privacy-NER Attention:} Achieved 99\% accuracy with minimal false positives and negatives, demonstrating strong performance on the synthetic test set.
  
  \item \textbf{Model Comparison:} Both Privacy-NER Attention and DeBERTa Fine-tuned achieved 98\% accuracy, significantly outperforming the zero-shot baseline (62\%). The Privacy-NER model showed slightly better performance on Not PII class.
  
  \item \textbf{Error Patterns:} Privacy-NER Attention had only 7 total misclassifications compared to DeBERTa's 12 and the baseline's 113 errors.
  
  \item \textbf{Architecture Benefits:} Both supervised approaches showed excellent performance, suggesting that while the specialized Privacy-NER architecture offers slight advantages for Not PII detection, standard fine-tuning of powerful pre-trained models can also achieve strong results.
\end{itemize}

